; The Melange build, enabled by UNLZ4_MELANGE=true (make test-melange).
;
; Dune cannot make a library's `modes` conditional, and declaring melange mode would put melc rules
; into @all on every build, including release builds and OCaml versions without Melange. So each
; library appears twice: once in its own directory (native and bytecode, disabled when
; UNLZ4_MELANGE=true) and once under melange/ (Melange only, enabled only then), copy_files'ing
; the very same sources.
